    "raw": "\\*Marcasite metastable above 673 K. Data extrapolated above 700 K. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-1000 K: $Cp^{\\circ} = 16.255 + 3.792 \\times 10^{-3} T - 2.199 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{0}-H_{298}^{0}=16.255\\times10^{-3}T+1.896\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+2.199\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-5.753$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-1000 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -74.010 + 8.133 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} - 4.495 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 380.100 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -74.010 - 8.133 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} + 4.495 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 190.050 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} + 102.081 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSource: Data from Chase (17) who extrapolated above 700 K. ",
